# Playwright Framework Architecture Rules

## Project Stack
- Playwright with TypeScript
- Page Object Model (POM)
- Separate Locator files
- Fixtures-based test data
- AI-DLC Pipeline for .docx → Playwright test generation
- Target: AML application at `https://kadelamldev.customerxps.com:2506` — login required

## File Creation Order for Any New Feature

New work goes under `tests/milestone2/` only (same layout as milestone1). Do not use `tests/e2e/`.

When creating a new feature (e.g., Exception List Manager under ConfigurationModule):

1. Create Spec File first
   - Location: `tests/milestone2/test-cases/<Module>/<feature>Tests/`
   - Naming: `feature-name.spec.ts` (e.g. `exception-list-manager.spec.ts`)

2. Create Locator File
   - Location: `tests/milestone2/objectrepositories/` (per-milestone; never `tests/objectrepositories/`)
   - Naming: `FeatureLocators.ts` (e.g. `ExceptionListManagerLocators.ts`)

3. Create Page Object File
   - Location: `tests/milestone2/pages/<Module>/<Feature>Pages/`
   - Naming: `FeaturePage.ts` (e.g. `ExceptionListManagerPage.ts`)
   - Import locators as `../../../objectrepositories/<Feature>Locators` from `pages/<Module>/<Feature>Pages/`

## Responsibilities

Spec File:
- Contains only test cases
- Calls page object methods
- Does NOT contain raw selectors
- Does NOT contain business logic

Locator File:
- Contains only element locators
- No Playwright commands
- Export as object

Page Object File:
- Imports locator file
- Create getters for locators
- Contains reusable action methods
- No assertions unless validation-specific method

Never mix responsibilities.
